## Conclusion (Measured)
# When a main-frame load fails while the WebView holds a page that had loaded (2, 3, 8: reload, Retry, and by the same
# mechanism system Back into history, API-08-05), WebView 124 calls onPageFinished twice for the failed navigation.
# MainFrameLoadOutcome.onFinished() resets the mark on the first, so the second reports loaded=true; onPageLoaded ->
# showPage() makes the WebView VISIBLE with Chromium's error page, which prints the URL, and removes the overlay and its
# Retry. When the WebView holds no loaded page (first load, or after an earlier failure: 4, 5, 6), there is one finish
# and the design holds; that is the only state IMP-12 exercised. The error kind (refused -6, dropped -1) does not matter.
# DS-006's premise "onPageFinished always ends a main-frame load (once)" holds only for the second state.
